## THE SINGLE ARCHITECTURAL TRUTH

Git never scans. Git never re-reads unchanged files. Git never re-verifies what it already knows.

Git snapshots the tree at every commit and computes deltas between snapshots.

Synapse must work identically:

```
Init             = Commit Zero. Full scan. One time only. Never again.
Every commit after = Git delta. Process only what changed. Always fast.
Rollback         = Restore a previous snapshot. Instant.
Branch switch    = Load that branch's snapshot. Instant.
```

The index is not a separate system that watches Git.
The index is a different projection of the same Git history.

This is the only architectural principle you need. Everything else follows from it.

